# Pulse business flows

```yaml
businessFlows:
  - id: protected-checkout
    name: Protected checkout remains available during a surge
    description: A shopper submits checkout traffic while Pulse may be degrading non-critical work; checkout must remain normal and fast at every shedding tier.
    entryPoints:
      - POST /checkout
    criticality: high

  - id: recommendation-degradation
    name: Recommendations degrade before critical traffic
    description: Recommendations serve normally at level 0, disable at levels 1 and 2, and become emergency-rate-limited at level 3.
    entryPoints:
      - GET /recommendations
    criticality: medium

  - id: catalog-cache-fallback
    name: Catalog uses a stale cache under sustained load
    description: Catalog remains normal through level 1, serves a simplified stale response at level 2, and is rate-limited with cached fallback at level 3.
    entryPoints:
      - GET /catalog
    criticality: medium

  - id: shedding-control
    name: Pulse changes the protected application's load-shedding tier
    description: An authenticated internal caller changes a reversible tier with correlation, reasoning, and signal evidence; the transition is persisted before activation.
    entryPoints:
      - POST /internal/load-shedding
    criticality: high

  - id: protected-application-observability
    name: Pulse reads protected-application health and traffic
    description: The agent and operators read durable tier readiness, active endpoint policy, rolling request rate, latency, errors, concurrency, and fixed-cardinality endpoint counts.
    entryPoints:
      - GET /health
      - GET /metrics/snapshot
    criticality: high

  - id: agent-readiness
    name: Operators receive truthful dependency and worker readiness
    description: The agent lifespan starts bounded workers and an always-running dependency supervisor; database or mandatory-worker failure returns 503 while task liveness and health details remain visible, and readiness returns to 200 after in-process recovery.
    entryPoints:
      - GET agent /health
      - agent/app/main.py lifespan
      - agent/app/workers/dependencies.py
      - agent/app/workers/realtime.py
    criticality: high

  - id: simulated-leading-signal-ingestion
    name: A deterministic run supplies bounded leading signals
    description: An authenticated load driver submits expiring, run-attributed simulated edge, queue, session, login, or CPU readings; duplicates, expired frames, unavailable workers, and full buffers fail explicitly.
    entryPoints:
      - POST /internal/signals/simulated
    criticality: high

  - id: realtime-surge-detection
    name: Pulse detects an unannounced acceleration surge
    description: The realtime worker joins origin and optional leading signals, applies bounded baseline/acceleration/ratio/confidence confirmation with hysteresis, persists the snapshot and prediction, and submits immutable protection intent without dying during transient active-run database outages.
    entryPoints:
      - agent/app/workers/realtime.py
      - agent/app/detection/realtime.py
      - load_tests/scenarios/sudden_spike.py
    criticality: high

  - id: scheduled-prewarm
    name: Pulse prewarms for a scheduled Diwali event
    description: The scheduled worker loads active calendar events, validates timezone and UTC bounds, builds monotonic bounded ramp steps, persists predictions, audits obsolete restart points, and sends only the latest safe due target.
    entryPoints:
      - agent/app/workers/scheduled.py
      - agent/app/services/ramp_planner.py
      - scripts/seed_scheduled_events.py
      - load_tests/scenarios/scheduled_diwali.py
    criticality: high

  - id: unified-protection-arbitration
    name: Scheduled and realtime intent share one protected mutation path
    description: A serialized cross-mode arbiter refreshes authoritative capacity and tier state, prefers protection over hold/recovery, retains maximum active requirements, double-clamps ceilings, durably claims the complete action/tier outbox, then invokes the sole ASG adapter and authenticated tier client.
    entryPoints:
      - agent/app/orchestration/response_pipeline.py
      - agent/app/aws/autoscaling.py
      - agent/app/services/shedding_client.py
    criticality: high

  - id: gradual-recovery
    name: Pulse unwinds protection only after sustained low load
    description: Distinct persisted low snapshots feed one recovery coordinator across realtime, scheduled, and maintenance callers; recovery alone may decrease one bounded capacity/tier step, respects floor and cooldown, and yields immediately to renewed protection.
    entryPoints:
      - agent/app/orchestration/recovery.py
      - agent/app/orchestration/realtime_lifecycle.py
      - agent/app/workers/maintenance.py
    criticality: high

  - id: durable-maintenance
    name: Pulse reconciles and resumes incomplete control work
    description: The bounded maintenance loop checks mandatory dependencies, reconciles unknown capacity outcomes, retries pending dispatch/tier stages with original correlation, resumes durable tier outbox work without repeating capacity, and prunes old snapshots in bounded batches.
    entryPoints:
      - agent/app/workers/maintenance.py
      - agent/app/orchestration/reconciliation.py
      - db/repositories/response_retries.py
      - db/repositories/scaling_actions.py
      - db/repositories/snapshots.py
    criticality: high

  - id: demo-run-evidence-lifecycle
    name: Load runs persist reproducible configuration and results
    description: An authenticated runner idempotently starts and completes a run with pair identity, workload seed/weights, server-sanitized effective settings, thresholds, execution mode, Locust summary, formula version, and record references; completed runs are evaluated from persisted evidence only.
    entryPoints:
      - POST /internal/demo-runs
      - PATCH /internal/demo-runs/{run_id}
      - load_tests/scripts/run_scenario.py
      - load_tests/scripts/run_pair.py
      - agent/app/services/feedback.py
    criticality: high

  - id: operator-dashboard
    name: Operators inspect bounded control and result history
    description: The read-only dashboard polls status and bounded paginated history, consumes explicit pulse.snapshot.v1 capacity fields with derived pending capacity, overlays predictions/actions/actuals, and never receives a control credential.
    entryPoints:
      - GET /api/v1/status
      - GET /api/v1/snapshots
      - GET /api/v1/predictions
      - GET /api/v1/predictions/{prediction_id}
      - GET /api/v1/scaling-actions
      - GET /api/v1/load-shedding-events
      - GET /api/v1/scheduled-events
      - dashboard/components/Dashboard.tsx
      - dashboard/lib/api.ts
    criticality: high

  - id: result-review-and-export
    name: Operators review defensible surge outcomes
    description: Result routes and the export script expose checkout latency/success, detection lead, provisioning efficiency, prediction/cost/recovery evidence, formulas, warnings, and bounded record references; missing evidence remains not_available rather than invented.
    entryPoints:
      - GET /api/v1/results/summary
      - GET /api/v1/results/runs/{run_id}
      - scripts/export_results.py
      - docs/results-template.md
    criticality: medium

  - id: optional-live-aws-capacity
    name: An operator enables bounded live ASG capacity control
    description: After a reviewed Terraform plan/apply and explicit live configuration, Pulse reads the named ASG and invokes resource-scoped SetDesiredCapacity. Validated scale-out bypasses ASG cooldown, recovery scale-in honors it, and dry-run never constructs AWS clients.
    entryPoints:
      - infra/
      - agent/app/aws/autoscaling.py
      - agent/app/metrics/providers/cloudwatch.py
      - agent/app/metrics/providers/sqs.py
    criticality: high

  - id: clean-stack-delivery-verification
    name: GitHub Actions verifies the complete local platform
    description: Push and PR workflows compile/lint/test Python with coverage, cycle PostgreSQL migrations, test/build the dashboard, build a credential-free Compose stack, run scheduled and sudden Locust smoke, validate Terraform/IAM/cost constraints, and scan secrets/artifacts/diff hygiene.
    entryPoints:
      - .github/workflows/ci.yml
      - scripts/smoke_stack.sh
      - scripts/verify_smoke_results.py
      - scripts/secret_scan.py
    criticality: high
```
